1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:02,081
Part five:

2
00:00:02,131 --> 00:00:04,118
what iFIX enables.

3
00:00:05,668 --> 00:00:08,405
When systems post fiscal events to iFIX,

4
00:00:08,455 --> 00:00:13,213
any authorised viewer can see the status
of funds across all of them.

5
00:00:13,263 --> 00:00:16,070
How much an entity has and where it sits.

6
00:00:16,120 --> 00:00:20,808
What it is meant for, and whether each
expense is planned or ad hoc,

7
00:00:20,858 --> 00:00:22,968
committed or awaiting approval.

8
00:00:23,018 --> 00:00:26,731
What was spent, what it produced, and who
approved it.

9
00:00:26,781 --> 00:00:30,493
Utilisation certificates can become
flexible controls,

10
00:00:30,543 --> 00:00:33,699
with tranches released on verified
milestones.

11
00:00:33,749 --> 00:00:39,482
And idle balances become visible, so they
can be reallocated and borrowing reduced.

12
00:00:41,032 --> 00:00:45,376
Tax revenue is the product of coverage,
collection and valuation.

13
00:00:45,426 --> 00:00:48,013
Shared registries help expand coverage:

14
00:00:48,063 --> 00:00:52,069
a property appears in water, power,
licence and tax records,

15
00:00:52,119 --> 00:00:54,368
so missing entries become visible.

16
00:00:54,418 --> 00:00:59,506
Estimate events set collection targets,
and receipts show who achieves them.

17
00:00:59,556 --> 00:01:04,508
And a unified front-end can show a citizen
everything due on a property or

18
00:01:04,558 --> 00:01:09,038
business, so fewer bills go unpaid simply
because they were missed.

19
00:01:10,588 --> 00:01:15,074
Today, estimates and actual revenues or
expenditures can vary widely,

20
00:01:15,124 --> 00:01:19,479
bringing disrupted schedules, skipped
maintenance, and shock bills:

21
00:01:19,529 --> 00:01:22,042
large liabilities that nobody forecast.

22
00:01:22,092 --> 00:01:25,001
With revenues and expenses flowing as
events,

23
00:01:25,051 --> 00:01:28,025
surpluses and shortfalls become visible
early,

24
00:01:28,075 --> 00:01:33,218
and forecasting models can correct the
estimates made at the start of the year.

25
00:01:34,768 --> 00:01:35,722
A live example.

26
00:01:35,772 --> 00:01:40,878
Punjab's Department of Water Supply and
Sanitation had no visibility into the

27
00:01:40,928 --> 00:01:45,030
electricity and maintenance costs of
village water committees,

28
00:01:45,080 --> 00:01:47,106
nor into their fee collections.

29
00:01:47,156 --> 00:01:47,843
The result:

30
00:01:47,893 --> 00:01:51,258
large unpaid electricity bills landing at
year end.

31
00:01:51,308 --> 00:01:55,074
The department rolled out a logging app to
every village.

32
00:01:55,124 --> 00:01:56,815
Operators record expenses;

33
00:01:56,865 --> 00:01:59,561
bill collectors record fees door to door.

34
00:01:59,611 --> 00:02:05,052
iFIX collates these into a real-time dashboard
of each village's financial health,

35
00:02:05,102 --> 00:02:09,806
and integration with the power company is
adding billing data directly.

36
00:02:11,356 --> 00:02:15,035
In a federal system, planning should start
from the bottom.

37
00:02:15,085 --> 00:02:19,460
Too often it is incremental, and plans are
retrofitted to the numbers.

38
00:02:19,510 --> 00:02:23,379
With a department's expenditures and
outputs recorded in iFIX,

39
00:02:23,429 --> 00:02:27,615
last year's actuals become the benchmark
for next year's estimates,

40
00:02:27,665 --> 00:02:30,712
plan and estimate events can cite their
evidence,

41
00:02:30,762 --> 00:02:33,746
and legislatures can debate proposals with
data.

42
00:02:35,296 --> 00:02:39,937
Timely payment of vendors is one of the
highest-friction areas of PFM.

43
00:02:39,987 --> 00:02:45,432
Smart contracts can pay automatically once
the works system certifies a milestone,

44
00:02:45,482 --> 00:02:48,716
cutting the administrative load on finance
teams.

45
00:02:48,766 --> 00:02:49,855
Scrutiny remains:

46
00:02:49,905 --> 00:02:52,670
pilots with selected entities and vendors,

47
00:02:52,720 --> 00:02:57,830
and payments that only follow the earlier
plan, estimate and sanction checks.

48
00:02:59,380 --> 00:03:04,516
Accounting and audit are where the most
effort goes into chasing and reconciling

49
00:03:04,566 --> 00:03:05,294
information.

50
00:03:05,344 --> 00:03:09,573
With events in one place, information is
searchable and traceable,

51
00:03:09,623 --> 00:03:11,907
much of accounting can be automated,

52
00:03:11,957 --> 00:03:15,083
and an auditor can sample events and
verify them.

53
00:03:15,133 --> 00:03:18,713
Every change goes through an API, by an
authorised user,

54
00:03:18,763 --> 00:03:21,890
into a log that shows who changed what,
and when.

55
00:03:23,440 --> 00:03:26,087
Perhaps the most transformative
possibility:

56
00:03:26,137 --> 00:03:30,869
linking every expenditure to the outputs
and outcomes it was meant to achieve.

57
00:03:30,919 --> 00:03:35,895
Output and outcome budgets consolidate that
across projects, entities and schemes,

58
00:03:35,945 --> 00:03:38,409
support comparison on cost-effectiveness,

59
00:03:38,459 --> 00:03:43,190
and show whether welfare programmes
reached the people they were designed for.

60
00:03:45,190 --> 00:03:45,588
Next:

61
00:03:45,638 --> 00:03:49,172
putting the reimagination into practice.
